@*
    ViewAsHeaderControl — the right-aligned page-header "View as…" affordance.

    D-PLACE (locked 2026-08-11) specified TWO entry points: this one and the rail avatar-menu item.
    Only the rail item shipped in Sprint 6, which left the feature reachable solely through a popover
    at the bottom of a 64px rail — the user could not find it at all. Added in Sprint 6.5.

    Reference comp: SPEC/mockups/comp-c-review-10-view-as.html — a right-aligned trigger in the page
    header, described there as present "on every screen".

    Rendered once by MainLayout rather than by each of the 14 pages that own a .pagehead. That is
    what makes "every screen" true by construction instead of by 14 copies staying in sync, and it
    is why the control is positioned against the header band rather than sitting in its flow.
    It anchors to the crumbs line, which is empty on every page — BoardDetail is the only page with
    right-side header content and that picker sits lower, aligned to the bottom of the header row.

    Visibility is the caller's decision (MainLayout's _canViewAs): privileged role AND no session
    already running. Those are mutually exclusive with ViewAsBanner, so the two never both occupy
    the top of the page.
*@

<div class="viewas-anchor">
    <button class="viewas-trigger" type="button" @onclick="OnOpen" title="Browse Collega as another user">
        <FluentIcon Value="@(new Icons.Regular.Size16.Eye())" aria-hidden="true" />
        <span>View as…</span>
    </button>
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter] public EventCallback OnOpen { get; set; }
}
